module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.EventualSurjective
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Homogeneous
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A graded ring generated in degree one is a closed subscheme of projective space

Let `S = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} S_d` be a graded ring, let `R` be a commutative ring mapping into `S_0`, and
let `x_0, …, x_n ∈ S_1` generate `S` as an `R`-algebra. The `R`-algebra map
`R[T_0, …, T_n] → S`, `T_i ↦ x_i`, is then a homomorphism of graded rings which is **surjective
in every degree**: a homogeneous element of degree `d` is a polynomial in the `x_i` with
coefficients in `R`, and taking the degree-`d` part of that polynomial exhibits it as the image
of a homogeneous polynomial of degree `d`.

Stacks Tag 01N0 applies: the induced morphism is defined on all of `Proj S` and is a closed
immersion. So **`Proj S` is a closed subscheme of `ℙⁿ_R = Proj R[T_0, …, T_n]`**, which is the
statement this file carries.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.polyGradedHom`: the graded ring homomorphism
  `R[T_0, …, T_n] → S` determined by `T_i ↦ x_i`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.projToProjectiveSpace`: **the morphism
  `Proj S ⟶ ℙⁿ_R`** it induces, read on all of `Proj S` rather than on the domain of definition
  of Stacks Tag 01MY, which is everything here.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.aeval_mem_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule`: evaluating
  a homogeneous polynomial of degree `d` at degree-one elements gives an element of `S_d`, which
  is what makes the evaluation map graded.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.surjective_gradedAddHom_polyGradedHom`: **the
  evaluation map is surjective in every degree**, which is where generation in degree one is
  spent.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpace`: the
  morphism `Proj S ⟶ ℙⁿ_R` is a closed immersion.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpaceGradeZero`:
  **Stacks Tag 01N0 for a polynomial ring**, the same statement with `R = S_0`, which is the
  source's hypothesis "`S` is generated by `S_1` over `S_0`" verbatim.

## Implementation notes

**Degreewise surjectivity, not surjectivity of a span.** The hypothesis is that the `x_i`
generate `S` as an `R`-algebra, so `Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range x) = ⊤`; by
`Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval` the evaluation map is surjective. Surjectivity *in each
degree* needs one more step, and it is the uniqueness of the homogeneous decomposition: writing
a preimage `p` of `s ∈ S_d` as the sum of its homogeneous components, the images of those
components are homogeneous of the matching degrees, so applying `GradedRing.proj S d` to the
identity `s = ∑_e aeval x (p_e)` leaves `s = aeval x (p_d)`. The degree-`d` component of a
preimage is therefore a homogeneous preimage, and no finiteness or Noetherian hypothesis enters.

**The base ring is left free, and `S_0` is a special case.** Nothing below needs `R → S_0` to be
an isomorphism, or even injective; only that it lands in degree zero, which is what makes the
evaluation map graded. Taking `R = S_0` with the inclusion recovers the source's hypothesis, and
that instance is `isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpaceGradeZero`; the ring structure on `S_0`
is `SetLike.GradeZero.instCommRing`, declared as a local instance there because the degree-zero
part of a variable grading is not found by instance search inside the polynomial ring's own
`Module` and `AddSubgroupClass` instances.

**Projective space is in its `Proj` presentation.** `ℙⁿ_R` is written as
`Proj R[T_0, …, T_n]`, which is how the source introduces it (Stacks Tag 01ND); the repository's
`AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveSpaceOverRing` is instead the base change of `ℙⁿ_ℤ` from Stacks
Definition 01NF, and the identification of the two is Stacks Tag 01N2, which this repository does
not carry. No such identification is used or claimed here.

**Which clause of Tag 01N0 this is.** Tag 01N0 is a three-part statement about the triple
`(U(ψ), r_ψ, θ)` of Stacks Tag 01MY, and its parts (1) and (2) for an arbitrary graded
homomorphism surjective in all large degrees are
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.mapDomain_eq_top_of_eventually_surjective` and
`isClosedImmersion_projMapData_hom_of_eventually_surjective`. What is added here is part (2) at
the polynomial ring — the shape in which the tag is used to realise `Proj S` as a closed
subscheme of projective space — and the attribute below is scoped by its clause string to exactly
that. Part (3), the surjectivity of the comparison maps `θ : r_ψ^* 𝒪(n) ⟶ 𝒪(n)`, is not proved
anywhere in this repository and is not claimed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ND](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ND)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Filter
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistChain

universe u w

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

section Base

variable {S R : Type u} [CommRing S] [CommRing R] [Algebra R S]
  {τ : Type w} [SetLike τ S] [AddSubgroupClass τ S] (𝒮 : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒮]
  (halg : ∀ r : R, algebraMap R S r ∈ 𝒮 0) {n : ℕ} (x : Fin (n + 1) → S)
  (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ 𝒮 1)

include halg hx

/-- **Evaluating a homogeneous polynomial of degree `d` at degree-one elements lands in `S_d`.**
A monomial of total degree `d` becomes a product of `d` elements of `S_1` scaled by a coefficient
from `R`, which lies in degree zero. -/
theorem aeval_mem_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule {d : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R}
    (hp : p ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R d) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval x p ∈ 𝒮 d := by
  rw [MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule] at hp
  rw [MvPolynomial.aeval_def, MvPolynomial.eval₂_eq]
  refine sum_mem fun e he => ?_
  have hdeg : ∑ j ∈ e.support, e j • (1 : ℕ) = d := by
    have h := hp (MvPolynomial.mem_support_iff.mp he)
    rwa [Finsupp.weight_apply] at h
  have hprod : ∏ j ∈ e.support, x j ^ e j ∈ 𝒮 d := by
    have h := SetLike.prod_pow_mem_graded 𝒮 (fun _ : Fin (n + 1) => (1 : ℕ)) x
      (F := e.support) e fun k _ => hx k
    rwa [hdeg] at h
  have h := SetLike.mul_mem_graded (halg (MvPolynomial.coeff e p)) hprod
  simpa using h

/-- **The graded ring homomorphism `R[T_0, …, T_n] → S` sending `T_i` to `x_i`.** It is the
`R`-algebra evaluation map, graded because the `x_i` have degree one and the coefficients lie in
degree zero. -/
def polyGradedHom : MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R →+*ᵍ 𝒮 where
  toRingHom := (MvPolynomial.aeval x).toRingHom
  map_mem := aeval_mem_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule 𝒮 halg x hx

/-- **The evaluation map is surjective in every degree**, when the `x_i` generate `S` as an
`R`-algebra.

The evaluation map is surjective by `Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval`; a preimage `p` of
`s ∈ S_d` is the sum of its homogeneous components, whose images are homogeneous of the matching
degrees, so the degree-`d` projection of the identity `s = ∑_e aeval x (p_e)` identifies `s` with
the image of the single homogeneous component `p_d`. -/
theorem surjective_gradedAddHom_polyGradedHom (hgen : Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range x) = ⊤)
    (d : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective ((polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx).gradedAddHom d) := by
  classical
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := R) x) := by
    intro s
    have hmem : s ∈ (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := R) x).range := by
      rw [← Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval, hgen]
      trivial
    exact hmem
  rintro ⟨s, hs⟩
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hsurj s
  set M := p.totalDegree + 1 with hM
  set y : ℕ → S := fun e => MvPolynomial.aeval x (MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent e p) with hy
  have hymem : ∀ e, y e ∈ 𝒮 e := fun e =>
    aeval_mem_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule 𝒮 halg x hx (MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent_mem e p)
  have hsum : s = ∑ e ∈ Finset.range M, y e := by
    rw [hy, ← hp, ← map_sum, MvPolynomial.sum_homogeneousComponent]
  have hproj : GradedRing.proj 𝒮 d s = s := by
    rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒮 hs]
  have hprojy : ∀ e, GradedRing.proj 𝒮 d (y e) = if e = d then y e else 0 := by
    intro e
    by_cases he : e = d
    · subst he
      rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒮 (hymem e)]
      simp
    · rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒮 (hymem e) he]
      simp [he]
  refine ⟨⟨MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent d p, MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent_mem d p⟩,
    Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  show MvPolynomial.aeval x (MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent d p) = s
  rw [← hproj, hsum, map_sum]
  simp only [hprojy]
  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq' (Finset.range M) d y]
  split_ifs with hd
  · rfl
  · have hz : MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent d p = 0 :=
      MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent_eq_zero d p (by
        simp only [Finset.mem_range, hM] at hd
        omega)
    rw [hz, map_zero]

/-- Degreewise surjectivity in the eventual form that Stacks Tag 01N0 asks for. -/
theorem eventually_surjective_polyGradedHom (hgen : Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range x) = ⊤) :
    ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in atTop,
      Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom (polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx) d) :=
  Filter.Eventually.of_forall (surjective_gradedAddHom_polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx hgen)

/-- **The morphism `Proj S ⟶ ℙⁿ_R = Proj R[T_0, …, T_n]`** induced by `T_i ↦ x_i`. It is the
morphism of Stacks Tag 01MY, whose domain of definition is all of `Proj S` by part (1) of Stacks
Tag 01N0, transported to `Proj S` along that identification. -/
def projToProjectiveSpace (hgen : Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range x) = ⊤) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮 ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) :=
  (Scheme.topIso (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)).inv ≫
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮).isoOfEq
      (mapDomain_eq_top_of_eventually_surjective _ 𝒮 (polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx)
        (eventually_surjective_polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx hgen))).inv ≫
    mapHom _ 𝒮 (polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx)

/-- **`Proj S` is a closed subscheme of `ℙⁿ_R`.** The evaluation map is surjective in every
degree, so Stacks Tag 01N0 part (2)
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.isClosedImmersion_mapHom_of_eventually_surjective`)
makes the induced morphism a closed immersion; the two identifications prefixed to it in
`projToProjectiveSpace` are isomorphisms. -/
@[ega "II 2.9.2" "(i), special case", ega "II 2.9.5" "finite free M"]
theorem isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpace (hgen : Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range x) = ⊤) :
    IsClosedImmersion (projToProjectiveSpace 𝒮 halg x hx hgen) := by
  have h := isClosedImmersion_mapHom_of_eventually_surjective
    (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) 𝒮 (polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx)
    (eventually_surjective_polyGradedHom 𝒮 halg x hx hgen)
  rw [projToProjectiveSpace]
  infer_instance

end Base

section GradeZero

variable {S : Type u} [CommRing S] {τ : Type w} [SetLike τ S] [AddSubgroupClass τ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒮] {n : ℕ}

attribute [local instance] SetLike.GradeZero.instCommRing

/-- **Stacks Tag 01N0 at a polynomial ring: a graded ring generated in degree one by `n + 1`
elements is a closed subscheme of `ℙⁿ`.** Let `S` be a graded ring and let `x_0, …, x_n ∈ S_1`
generate `S` as an `S_0`-algebra. Then the induced morphism
`Proj S ⟶ ℙⁿ_{S_0} = Proj S_0[T_0, …, T_n]` is a closed immersion.

This is the source's hypothesis "`S` is generated by `S_1` over `S_0`" together with a choice of
`n + 1` generators, and it is `isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpace` with `R = S_0` and the
inclusion of the degree-zero part as the structure map. -/
@[stacks 01N0 "part (2) at a polynomial ring: closed immersion into ℙⁿ",
  ega "II 2.9.5" "special case"]
theorem isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpaceGradeZero (x : Fin (n + 1) → S)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ 𝒮 1) (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range x) = ⊤) :
    IsClosedImmersion
      (projToProjectiveSpace 𝒮 (R := (𝒮 0)) (fun r => r.2) x hx hgen) :=
  isClosedImmersion_projToProjectiveSpace 𝒮 _ x hx hgen

end GradeZero

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain

end
